<article>
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated <span class="ph">[go-live date]</span> · <a href="/da/cookies" hreflang="da">Dansk version</a></p>

    <section class="short" aria-labelledby="short-h">
      <h2 id="short-h">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We only store what you need to sign in and stay signed in.</li>
        <li>No tracking, no analytics, no advertising cookies, and nothing from other companies.</li>
        <li>That's why you don't see a cookie banner.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2 id="none">Why there's no banner</h2>
    <p>Danish rules on cookies (cookiebekendtgørelsen) require consent for storing information in your browser, except when it is
      strictly necessary for a service you asked for. Everything Kupro stores is needed to sign you in and keep your session secure,
      so no consent is needed. If we ever add something that does need consent, we will ask first, with "Reject" as easy as "Accept".</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p>Set by our sign-in server (Keycloak, hosted by us at auth.kupro.app). They are first-party, and never shared.</p>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mono">AUTH_SESSION_ID<br>KC_AUTH_SESSION_HASH</td><td>Keeps track of a sign-in while it is in progress</td><td>End of session</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">KC_RESTART</td><td>Lets a sign-in continue if it was interrupted</td><td>End of session</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">KEYCLOAK_IDENTITY<br>KEYCLOAK_SESSION</td><td>Keeps you signed in, so you don't type your password on every visit</td><td>End of session, or up to 90 days (30 days without use) with "Remember me"</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">KEYCLOAK_LOCALE</td><td>Shows the sign-in page in the language you chose</td><td>End of session</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="draft"><b>Check before publishing:</b> confirm the exact names and lifetimes in the browser on production; they depend on the Keycloak version and realm settings.</p>

    <h2 id="storage">Browser storage</h2>
    <div class="tbl"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mono">oidc.user:…</td><td>Session storage</td><td>Your sign-in token for the Kupro app</td><td>When you close the tab</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono">oidc.…</td><td>Session storage</td><td>Short-lived check that protects the sign-in from forgery</td><td>When sign-in completes</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p>The public website itself stores nothing.</p>

    <h2 id="control">Your control</h2>
    <p>You can delete cookies and site data in your browser settings at any time. You'll be signed out and need to sign in again.
      Questions: <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a>.</p>
  </article>
